# The building's passenger lifts, declared as the assets they are.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The graph held `bldg:status_lift_0 ontosage:statusOf bldg:Lift_Main` and a detailed
# published description of the lift under `bldg:Cap_lift_accessibility_detail` -- and no
# triple anywhere declaring what `bldg:Lift_Main` IS. `asset_state_service._status_query`
# opens `?asset a ontosage:Lift`, so an untyped subject cannot match however many statuses
# name it, and "Is the lift working?" answered:
#
#     "This building has no lifts recorded in its model."
#
# about a lift the building describes in fifteen lines of surveyed detail. A confident
# false negative about data the building holds is what design contract 4 exists to
# prevent (BUG-438).
#
# HOW MANY LIFTS THERE ARE (BUG-497, settled by the building owner 2026-09-17)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO, one at each side of the building: `bldg:Lift_1` and `bldg:Lift_2`, both already
# declared in bldg1_abacws_metadata.ttl and typed brick:Elevator there. `bldg:Lift_Main`
# was a THIRD name for the same fabric, invented here so the status lane had a subject of
# type ontosage:Lift to match -- and the lane then answered "1 of 1 lift(s)" about a
# building with two. A vocabulary added to satisfy a query became a wrong count.
#
# So the two real assets carry the ontosage:Lift type (additively -- they keep
# brick:Elevator, which is what Brick-aware readers look for), and `Lift_Main` is gone as
# an asset. Its published accessibility description moves onto Lift_1, which is the lift
# that survey describes: "left from the front entrance".
#
# NOTHING HERE IS SIMULATED. Every fact below is transcribed from the same published
# accessibility survey that `Cap_lift_accessibility_detail` cites, so the lifts carry no
# ontosage:isSimulated flag -- only their live STATUS records do, and those live in the
# generated status file.

@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix brick:    <https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .
@prefix ontosage: <http://ontosage.org/capabilities#> .
@prefix bldg:     <http://abacwsbuilding.cardiff.ac.uk/abacws#> .

bldg:Lift_1 a ontosage:Lift , ontosage:Amenity ;
    rdfs:label "Passenger Lift 1"@en ;
    ontosage:capabilityCategory "Accessibility" ;
    ontosage:layTerms "lift, elevator, main lift, passenger lift, left lift, lift 1, is the lift working, lift status, is the elevator working" ;
    ontosage:locationText "Passenger Lift 1, left from the front entrance, approximately 25 m from the entrance; serves floors G, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5." ;
    ontosage:answerText "Passenger Lift 1 is located to the left of the front entrance, about 25 m in, and serves floors G, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. It has automatic double doors onto a lift lobby on every floor." ;
    ontosage:note "cardiff_university_accessibility_page" .

bldg:Lift_2 a ontosage:Lift , ontosage:Amenity ;
    rdfs:label "Passenger Lift 2 / Goods Lift"@en ;
    ontosage:capabilityCategory "Accessibility" ;
    ontosage:layTerms "second lift, goods lift, right lift, lift 2, other lift, service lift" ;
    ontosage:locationText "Passenger Lift 2, on the opposite side of the building from Lift 1; serves floors G, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 and takes goods as well as passengers." ;
    ontosage:answerText "Passenger Lift 2 is on the opposite side of the building from Lift 1 and serves floors G, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. It is the goods lift and is also sized for wheelchair use." ;
    ontosage:note "cardiff_university_accessibility_page" .

# The floors served are stated in the answer text above and NOT as ontosage:servesSpace
# triples: that property's declared domain is ontosage:ServedZone, so asserting it here
# would infer the lifts into a class they do not belong to. An undefined or misapplied
# predicate is how this project has previously acquired 56 mistyped instances -- the
# triple must be right, not merely present.
